</section>
<section id="S3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.4 </span>Cumulative Noise</h3>

<div id="S3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we analyze the cumulative noise generated under the proposed PrivateDFL framework for each communication round and compare it with the required noise needed to protect all training samples up to that round. To further highlight the benefit of PrivateDFL, we also contrast it with a black-box scenario, where noise contributions from previous clients and earlier communication rounds cannot be tracked, resulting in excessive noise being added to the HD model. We denote by <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{\gamma}_{r}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{\gamma}_{r}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> the cumulative noise after client <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> at round <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> under PrivateDFL, where prior contributions are explicitly accounted for. In contrast, <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{\Xi}_{K}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mi>K</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{\Xi}_{K}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the cumulative noise in the black-box setting, where past noise cannot be traced and the system redundantly adds new noise at each step.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For the first communication round, the noise applied by the first client is the same under both PrivateDFL and the black-box scenario. In this case, the required amount of noise is exactly satisfied, ensuring that the HD model is secured in either formulation. Formally, the cumulative noise <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{\gamma}_{1}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{\gamma}_{1}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> in PrivateDFL and the cumulative noise <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{\Xi}_{1}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{\Xi}_{1}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> in the black-box case coincide:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\vec{\gamma}_{1}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\vec{\gamma}_{1}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\vec{\Gamma}_{1}^{1}\sim\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\ln\!\left[\tfrac{1.25N}{\delta_{0}}\right]\right)=\vec{\xi}_{1}^{1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1.25</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\vec{\Gamma}_{1}^{1}\sim\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\ln\!\left[\tfrac{1.25N}{\delta_{0}}\right]\right)=\vec{\xi}_{1}^{1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\vec{\Xi}_{1}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\vec{\Xi}_{1}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\vec{\xi}_{1}^{1}\sim\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\ln\!\left[\tfrac{1.25N}{\delta_{0}}\right]\right)=\vec{\gamma}_{1}^{1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1.25</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\vec{\xi}_{1}^{1}\sim\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\ln\!\left[\tfrac{1.25N}{\delta_{0}}\right]\right)=\vec{\gamma}_{1}^{1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">For clients <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> in the first round, the cumulative noise at client <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> under PrivateDFL equals the required noise to protect the union of samples from the first <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> clients:</p>
<table id="S3.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\vec{\gamma}_{k}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\vec{\gamma}_{k}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{k}\vec{\Gamma}_{i}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{k}\vec{\Gamma}_{i}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\!\left(\ln\!\left[\tfrac{1.25N}{\delta_{0}}\right]+\sum_{i=2}^{k}\ln\!\left[\tfrac{i}{\,i-1\,}\right]\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1.25</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\!\left(\ln\!\left[\tfrac{1.25N}{\delta_{0}}\right]+\sum_{i=2}^{k}\ln\!\left[\tfrac{i}{\,i-1\,}\right]\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\ln\!\left[\tfrac{1.25N}{\delta_{0}}\prod_{i=2}^{k}\tfrac{i}{\,i-1\,}\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1.25</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\ln\!\left[\tfrac{1.25N}{\delta_{0}}\prod_{i=2}^{k}\tfrac{i}{\,i-1\,}\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\ln\!\left[\tfrac{1.25kN}{\delta_{0}}\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1.25</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\ln\!\left[\tfrac{1.25kN}{\delta_{0}}\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\vec{\xi}_{k}^{1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\vec{\xi}_{k}^{1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">For the black-box scenario, where prior perturbations cannot be tracked, the cumulative noise at client <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> in the first round equals the sum of the per-client required noises. Using independence of the zero-mean Gaussian terms, the variance parameters add:</p>
<table id="S3.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\vec{\Xi}_{k}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\vec{\Xi}_{k}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{k}\vec{\xi}_{i}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{k}\vec{\xi}_{i}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\sum_{i=1}^{k}\ln\!\left[\tfrac{1.25\,i\,N}{\delta_{0}}\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1.25</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\sum_{i=1}^{k}\ln\!\left[\tfrac{1.25\,i\,N}{\delta_{0}}\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\ln\!\left[\prod_{i=1}^{k}\tfrac{1.25\,i\,N}{\delta_{0}}\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mfrac><mrow><mn>1.25</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\ln\!\left[\prod_{i=1}^{k}\tfrac{1.25\,i\,N}{\delta_{0}}\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\ln\!\left[\left(\tfrac{1.25\,N}{\delta_{0}}\right)^{k}\,k!\right]\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1.25</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\ln\!\left[\left(\tfrac{1.25\,N}{\delta_{0}}\right)^{k}\,k!\right]\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\tfrac{1.25\,N}{\delta_{0}}&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1.25</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\tfrac{1.25\,N}{\delta_{0}}&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. The PrivateDFL variance factor for client <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> in round <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ln[kA]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ln[kA]</annotation></semantics></math>, whereas the black-box factor is <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\ln A+\ln(k!)=\ln\!\big[(A)^{k}k!\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\ln A+\ln(k!)=\ln\!\big[(A)^{k}k!\big]</annotation></semantics></math>. Since</p>
<table id="S3.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ln\!\big[(A)^{k}k!\big]-\ln[kA]=(k-1)\ln A+\ln\!\big((k-1)!\big)&gt;0\quad(k\geq 2)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ln\!\big[(A)^{k}k!\big]-\ln[kA]=(k-1)\ln A+\ln\!\big((k-1)!\big)&gt;0\quad(k\geq 2),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p5.3" class="ltx_p">the black-box cumulative noise is strictly larger than the PrivateDFL noise for all <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Aggregating the Gaussian increments from all <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> clients over the first <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r{-}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r{-}1</annotation></semantics></math> rounds and from the first <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> clients in round <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, and using telescoping of the logarithmic terms, we obtain the cumulative noise at client <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> in round <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\vec{\gamma}_{k}^{\,r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\vec{\gamma}_{k}^{\,r}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{r-1}\sum_{i=1}^{K}\vec{\Gamma}_{i}^{\,j}\;+\;\sum_{i=1}^{k}\vec{\Gamma}_{i}^{\,r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{r-1}\sum_{i=1}^{K}\vec{\Gamma}_{i}^{\,j}\;+\;\sum_{i=1}^{k}\vec{\Gamma}_{i}^{\,r}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}\!\Bigg(0,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\Bigg[\ln\!\Big[\tfrac{1.25N}{\delta_{0}}\Big]+\sum_{i=2}^{K}\ln\!\Big[\tfrac{i}{\,i-1\,}\Big]+\sum_{t=K}^{2K-1}\ln\!\Big[\tfrac{t+1}{t}\Big]+\cdots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∼</mo><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1.25</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋯</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}\!\Bigg(0,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\Bigg[\ln\!\Big[\tfrac{1.25N}{\delta_{0}}\Big]+\sum_{i=2}^{K}\ln\!\Big[\tfrac{i}{\,i-1\,}\Big]+\sum_{t=K}^{2K-1}\ln\!\Big[\tfrac{t+1}{t}\Big]+\cdots</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 71.00017pt+\sum_{t=K(r-2)+1}^{K(r-1)}\ln\!\Big[\tfrac{t+1}{t}\Big]+\sum_{t=K(r-1)}^{K(r-1)+k-1}\ln\!\Big[\tfrac{t+1}{t}\Big]\Bigg]\Bigg)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 71.00017pt+\sum_{t=K(r-2)+1}^{K(r-1)}\ln\!\Big[\tfrac{t+1}{t}\Big]+\sum_{t=K(r-1)}^{K(r-1)+k-1}\ln\!\Big[\tfrac{t+1}{t}\Big]\Bigg]\Bigg)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}\!\Bigg(0,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\ln\!\Bigg[\tfrac{1.25N}{\delta_{0}}\prod_{i=2}^{K}\tfrac{i}{\,i-1\,}\prod_{t=K}^{2K-1}\tfrac{t+1}{t}\cdots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∼</mo><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1.25</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mfrac><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">⋯</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}\!\Bigg(0,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\ln\!\Bigg[\tfrac{1.25N}{\delta_{0}}\prod_{i=2}^{K}\tfrac{i}{\,i-1\,}\prod_{t=K}^{2K-1}\tfrac{t+1}{t}\cdots</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 60.00009pt\prod_{t=K(r-2)+1}^{K(r-1)}\tfrac{t+1}{t}\prod_{t=K(r-1)}^{K(r-1)+k-1}\tfrac{t+1}{t}\Bigg]\Bigg)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mfrac><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></mfrac><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mfrac><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></mfrac><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 60.00009pt\prod_{t=K(r-2)+1}^{K(r-1)}\tfrac{t+1}{t}\prod_{t=K(r-1)}^{K(r-1)+k-1}\tfrac{t+1}{t}\Bigg]\Bigg)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\ln\!\Big[\tfrac{1.25\,\big(K(r-1)+k\big)\,N}{\delta_{0}}\Big]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1.25</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.710em" minsize="1.710em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.710em" minsize="1.710em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\ln\!\Big[\tfrac{1.25\,\big(K(r-1)+k\big)\,N}{\delta_{0}}\Big]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\vec{\xi}_{k}^{\,r}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\vec{\xi}_{k}^{\,r}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Setting <math id="S3.SS4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=R</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=K</annotation></semantics></math> yields the final cumulative noise after <math id="S3.SS4.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> rounds and <math id="S3.SS4.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> clients; we define</p>
<table id="S3.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{\gamma}_{K}^{\,R}\sim\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\;\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\,\ln\!\left[\tfrac{1.25\,KR\,N}{\delta_{0}}\right]\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mi>K</mi><mi>R</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1.25</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{\gamma}_{K}^{\,R}\sim\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\;\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\,\ln\!\left[\tfrac{1.25\,KR\,N}{\delta_{0}}\right]\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p7.2" class="ltx_p">which is the cumulative noise added to the HD model over <math id="S3.SS4.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> communication rounds by <math id="S3.SS4.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> clients to train the final secure model in the PrivateDFL algorithm.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS4.p8.1" class="ltx_p">We now derive the cumulative noise in the black-box scenario, where each client adds the full required noise <math id="S3.SS4.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{\xi}_{k}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{\xi}_{k}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> at every round without tracking what was already added in prior rounds. For client <math id="S3.SS4.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> at round <math id="S3.SS4.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, the cumulative noise is</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\vec{\Xi}_{k}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\vec{\Xi}_{k}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\vec{\xi}_{1}^{1}+\vec{\xi}_{2}^{1}+\cdots+\vec{\xi}_{K}^{1}+\vec{\xi}_{1}^{2}+\vec{\xi}_{2}^{2}+\cdots+\vec{\xi}_{K}^{2}+\cdots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mn>2</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋯</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\vec{\xi}_{1}^{1}+\vec{\xi}_{2}^{1}+\cdots+\vec{\xi}_{K}^{1}+\vec{\xi}_{1}^{2}+\vec{\xi}_{2}^{2}+\cdots+\vec{\xi}_{K}^{2}+\cdots</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\vec{\xi}_{1}^{r-1}+\vec{\xi}_{2}^{r-1}+\cdots+\vec{\xi}_{K}^{r-1}+\vec{\xi}_{1}^{r}+\vec{\xi}_{2}^{r}+\cdots+\vec{\xi}_{k}^{r}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\vec{\xi}_{1}^{r-1}+\vec{\xi}_{2}^{r-1}+\cdots+\vec{\xi}_{K}^{r-1}+\vec{\xi}_{1}^{r}+\vec{\xi}_{2}^{r}+\cdots+\vec{\xi}_{k}^{r}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS4.p10.1" class="ltx_p">From Proof <a href="#Thmproofthm4" title="Proof 4 ‣ 3.3 PrivateDFL ‣ 3 Research Methodology ‣ Privacy-Preserving Decentralized Federated Learning via Explainable Adaptive Differential Privacy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, the required noise for client <math id="S3.SS4.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> at round <math id="S3.SS4.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="S3.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{\xi}_{i}^{j}\sim\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\,\ln\!\left[\frac{1.25Nji}{\delta_{0}}\right]\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1.25</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{\xi}_{i}^{j}\sim\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\,\ln\!\left[\frac{1.25Nji}{\delta_{0}}\right]\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS4.p11.1" class="ltx_p">Substituting into the cumulative expression gives</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\vec{\Xi}_{k}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\vec{\Xi}_{k}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\ln\!\left[\tfrac{1.25N}{\delta_{0}}\right]\right)+\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\ln\!\left[\tfrac{1.25N\cdot 2}{\delta_{0}}\right]\right)+\cdots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1.25</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>1.25</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋯</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\ln\!\left[\tfrac{1.25N}{\delta_{0}}\right]\right)+\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\ln\!\left[\tfrac{1.25N\cdot 2}{\delta_{0}}\right]\right)+\cdots</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\ln\!\left[\tfrac{1.25N\cdot K}{\delta_{0}}\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>1.25</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\ln\!\left[\tfrac{1.25N\cdot K}{\delta_{0}}\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\ln\!\left[\tfrac{1.25N\cdot(K+1)}{\delta_{0}}\right]\right)+\cdots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>1.25</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋯</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\ln\!\left[\tfrac{1.25N\cdot(K+1)}{\delta_{0}}\right]\right)+\cdots</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\ln\!\left[\tfrac{1.25N(K(r-1)+k)}{\delta_{0}}\right]\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1.25</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\ln\!\left[\tfrac{1.25N(K(r-1)+k)}{\delta_{0}}\right]\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS4.p13.1" class="ltx_p">Collecting all terms, the cumulative noise at client <math id="S3.SS4.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> in round <math id="S3.SS4.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> becomes</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\vec{\Xi}_{k}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\vec{\Xi}_{k}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E34.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}\!\Bigg(0,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\,\Bigg[\sum_{t=1}^{K(r-1)+k}\ln\!\left(\tfrac{1.25Nt}{\delta_{0}}\right)\Bigg]\Bigg)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1.25</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}\!\Bigg(0,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\,\Bigg[\sum_{t=1}^{K(r-1)+k}\ln\!\left(\tfrac{1.25Nt}{\delta_{0}}\right)\Bigg]\Bigg).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS4.p15.1" class="ltx_p">This summation can be factorized into a product form:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\vec{\Xi}_{k}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\vec{\Xi}_{k}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}\!\Bigg(0,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\,\ln\!\Bigg[\prod_{t=1}^{K(r-1)+k}\tfrac{1.25Nt}{\delta_{0}}\Bigg]\Bigg)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mfrac><mrow><mn>1.25</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}\!\Bigg(0,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\,\ln\!\Bigg[\prod_{t=1}^{K(r-1)+k}\tfrac{1.25Nt}{\delta_{0}}\Bigg]\Bigg)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{N}\!\Bigg(0,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\,\ln\!\Bigg[\Bigl(\tfrac{1.25N}{\delta_{0}}\Bigr)^{K(r-1)+k}\times(K(r-1)+k)!\Bigg]\Bigg)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1.25</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{N}\!\Bigg(0,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\,\ln\!\Bigg[\Bigl(\tfrac{1.25N}{\delta_{0}}\Bigr)^{K(r-1)+k}\times(K(r-1)+k)!\Bigg]\Bigg).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS4.p17.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, setting <math id="S3.SS4.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=R</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS4.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=K</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain the total cumulative noise across <math id="S3.SS4.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> rounds and <math id="S3.SS4.p17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> clients:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p18" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\vec{\Xi}_{K}^{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mi>K</mi><mi>R</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\vec{\Xi}_{K}^{R}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}\!\Bigg(0,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\,\ln\!\Bigg[\Bigl(\tfrac{1.25N}{\delta_{0}}\Bigr)^{KR}\times(KR)!\Bigg]\Bigg)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1.25</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}\!\Bigg(0,\frac{2D}{\epsilon^{2}}\,\ln\!\Bigg[\Bigl(\tfrac{1.25N}{\delta_{0}}\Bigr)^{KR}\times(KR)!\Bigg]\Bigg).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p19" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS4.p19.1" class="ltx_p">This shows that in the black-box case the cumulative noise grows with <math id="S3.SS4.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(KR)!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(KR)!</annotation></semantics></math>, which is significantly larger than the controlled logarithmic growth in PrivateDFL.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Experimental Design</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate the effectiveness of PrivateDFL using three widely adopted benchmark datasets that span different modalities: MNIST (image-based), ISOLET (speech signal-based), and UCI-HAR (tabular sensor-based). This selection allows us to demonstrate the robustness of the proposed framework across heterogeneous data types. To assess data distribution effects, we consider both Independent and Identically Distributed (IID) and non-IID scenarios. In the IID case, data samples are divided uniformly across clients so that each client has an equal share of the global distribution. In contrast, the non-IID setting enforces data heterogeneity by restricting each client to only two classes; for instance, in MNIST, one client may receive only digits {0,1}, another {2,3}, and so on. This split reflects realistic IoT deployments where edge devices often collect skewed data.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Our evaluation follows a stepwise methodology. First, we conduct a sensitivity analysis to investigate how privacy parameters and HD model configurations influence PrivateDFL performance. We report accuracy and examine its dependence on the privacy budget <math id="S4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and privacy loss parameter <math id="S4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, the hypervector dimensionality <math id="S4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>, and the number of training samples per client under both IID and non-IID partitions. For the IID setting, we also vary the number of clients <math id="S4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> while keeping the total training data fixed, which isolates the effect of partitioning and highlights the trade off between coordination and performance.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Beyond internal sensitivity studies, we benchmark PrivateDFL against state-of-the-art Transformer-based and deep learning models trained with DP in centralized settings. These baseline models operate without federated constraints, accessing the complete dataset directly, and therefore represent the upper bound of achievable accuracy with minimal latency. We implement two privacy mechanisms, DP-SGD and RDP, using the Opacus library for PyTorch <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">49</a>]</cite>. For MNIST, we benchmark against vision architectures including Vision Transformer, ResNet50, GoogLeNet, and AlexNet. For ISOLET, we employ sequential models such as Transformer, Convolutional Neural Network (CNN), Recurrent Neural Network (RNN), and Temporal Convolutional Network (TCN). For UCI-HAR, we adopt tabular learning architectures including TabTransformer, TabNet, Deep Neural Network (DNN), and Deep and Cross Network (DCN). Comparisons are reported in terms of accuracy, training time, energy consumption, and inference latency, under a fixed privacy budget of <math id="S4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=0.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=0.4</annotation></semantics></math> and a privacy loss coefficient of <math id="S4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{0}=0.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{0}=0.001</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">All experiments are conducted in a controlled computing environment configured to emulate the constraints of edge devices while ensuring reproducibility. Each system is equipped with dual 32-core AMD EPYC 7513 processors, 512 GB of RAM, fast SSD storage, and an NVIDIA A100 GPU with 40 GB of memory, 6912 CUDA cores, and 1.6 TB/s memory bandwidth. While the hardware enables precise measurement of performance metrics, our optimization framework enforces strict limits on latency and energy consumption to mirror practical IoT scenarios. Random seeds are fixed for all runs, and energy and timing are recorded directly at the training and inference stages to provide accurate performance assessments.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Experimental Results</h2>

<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1 </span>Sensitivity Analysis</h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection, we examine how key hyperparameters including the privacy budget <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, the privacy loss parameter <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, the number of clients <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, the hypervector dimensionality <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>, and the number of training samples per client affect PrivateDFL accuracy. We begin with the privacy parameters under an IID split.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#S5.F5.sf1" title="In Figure 5 ‣ 5.1 Sensitivity Analysis ‣ 5 Experimental Results ‣ Privacy-Preserving Decentralized Federated Learning via Explainable Adaptive Differential Privacy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5(a)</span></a> shows test accuracy on MNIST when the training data are evenly partitioned across 100 clients under IID conditions. With a large privacy budget (for example, <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{0}=10^{-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{0}=10^{-3}</annotation></semantics></math>), the injected noise is small and accuracy reaches <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="96.34\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>96.34</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">96.34\%</annotation></semantics></math>. Fixing <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{0}=10^{-9}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{0}=10^{-9}</annotation></semantics></math> and decreasing <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> increases the noise magnitude and reduces accuracy; the curve drops from <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="96.14\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>96.14</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">96.14\%</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="95.62\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>95.62</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">95.62\%</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="94.23\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>94.23</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">94.23\%</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="93.65\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>93.65</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">93.65\%</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="89.78\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>89.78</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">89.78\%</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="87.32\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>87.32</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">87.32\%</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="75.16\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>75.16</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">75.16\%</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in\{0.5,0.1,0.05,0.01,0.005,0.001\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.05</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.01</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.005</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.001</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in\{0.5,0.1,0.05,0.01,0.005,0.001\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">By contrast, varying <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> has only a marginal effect. For instance, at <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=0.1</annotation></semantics></math>, tightening <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-3}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-18}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>18</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-18}</annotation></semantics></math> changes accuracy by about <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.56" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.56</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.56</annotation></semantics></math> percentage points (from <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="94.53\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>94.53</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">94.53\%</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="93.97\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>93.97</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">93.97\%</annotation></semantics></math>). Small fluctuations also appear due to randomness in noise draws across repeated runs; for example, at <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=0.5</annotation></semantics></math> the accuracy is <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="95.49\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>95.49</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">95.49\%</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{0}=10^{-12}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{0}=10^{-12}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="95.62\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>95.62</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">95.62\%</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{0}=10^{-9}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{0}=10^{-9}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="95.76\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>95.76</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">95.76\%</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{0}=10^{-15}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{0}=10^{-15}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is a difference of at most <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.27" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.27</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.27</annotation></semantics></math> percentage points. The same trends hold for ISOLET and UCI-HAR under IID conditions with 100 clients, as shown in Figures <a href="#S5.F5.sf2" title="In Figure 5 ‣ 5.1 Sensitivity Analysis ‣ 5 Experimental Results ‣ Privacy-Preserving Decentralized Federated Learning via Explainable Adaptive Differential Privacy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5(b)</span></a> and <a href="#S5.F5.sf3" title="In Figure 5 ‣ 5.1 Sensitivity Analysis ‣ 5 Experimental Results ‣ Privacy-Preserving Decentralized Federated Learning via Explainable Adaptive Differential Privacy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5(c)</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Figs. <a href="#S5.F5.sf4" title="In Figure 5 ‣ 5.1 Sensitivity Analysis ‣ 5 Experimental Results ‣ Privacy-Preserving Decentralized Federated Learning via Explainable Adaptive Differential Privacy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5(d)</span></a>, <a href="#S5.F5.sf5" title="In Figure 5 ‣ 5.1 Sensitivity Analysis ‣ 5 Experimental Results ‣ Privacy-Preserving Decentralized Federated Learning via Explainable Adaptive Differential Privacy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5(e)</span></a>, and <a href="#S5.F5.sf6" title="In Figure 5 ‣ 5.1 Sensitivity Analysis ‣ 5 Experimental Results ‣ Privacy-Preserving Decentralized Federated Learning via Explainable Adaptive Differential Privacy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5(f)</span></a> extend this analysis to the non-IID setting, continuing the trends observed under IID while revealing stronger sensitivity for MNIST due to client heterogeneity. At <math id="S5.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=0.5</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{0}=10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{0}=10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math>, MNIST accuracy declines from <math id="S5.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="95.81\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>95.81</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">95.81\%</annotation></semantics></math> under IID to <math id="S5.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="89.08\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>89.08</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">89.08\%</annotation></semantics></math> under non-IID. ISOLET and UCI-HAR show smaller gaps under the same parameters, with <math id="S5.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="88.01\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>88.01</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">88.01\%</annotation></semantics></math> versus <math id="S5.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="89.22\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>89.22</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">89.22\%</annotation></semantics></math> for ISOLET and <math id="S5.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="93.99\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>93.99</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">93.99\%</annotation></semantics></math> versus <math id="S5.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="92.09\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>92.09</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">92.09\%</annotation></semantics></math> for UCI-HAR.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.F5" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="S5.F5.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.10691v1/mnist_iid_acc_eps_delta.png" id="S5.F5.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:157/95;" width="157" height="95" alt="Refer to caption">
